BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Python's Conditional Branching Architecture \(if, if-else, if-elif-else\). Discuss block scoping rules and short-circuit evaluation in complex boolean expressions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundations of Conditional Execution:) Tj
T*
(   In computer programming, conditional execution enables dynamic decision-making by evaluating) Tj
T*
(   predicate expressions to determine execution flow.) Tj
T*
(   Python's conditional branching hierarchy consists of:) Tj
T*
(   - Simple if: Evaluates a boolean condition. If truthy, executes the indented suite; otherwise) Tj
T*
(   skips it.) Tj
T*
(   - if-else: Provides a binary branch: executes Branch 1 if condition is truthy, Branch 2 if) Tj
T*
(   falsy.) Tj
T*
(   - if-elif-else: Implements multi-way selection. Python tests conditions sequentially from top) Tj
T*
(   to bottom. As soon as a branch condition evaluates to True, its block executes, and all) Tj
T*
(   subsequent elif/else blocks are bypassed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Scope Rules in Python Conditionals:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike C/C++ or Java, Python code blocks demarcated by if, elif, else, for, or while do NOT) Tj
T*
(   introduce a new local scope!) Tj
T*
(   Any variable assigned inside an if block belongs to the enclosing function or module namespace.) Tj
T*
(   If the branch does not execute, accessing that variable later raises a NameError.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Short-Circuit Evaluation in Predicates:) Tj
T*
(   Compound conditional expressions utilizing and / or leverage short-circuiting:) Tj
T*
(   - In \(A and B and C\), evaluation terminates at the first falsy term.) Tj
T*
(   - In \(A or B or C\), evaluation terminates at the first truthy term.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Implementation & Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   def evaluate_tax_bracket\(annual_income: float\) -> dict:) Tj
T*
(   """Multi-way selection with input validation.""") Tj
T*
(   if annual_income < 0:) Tj
T*
(   raise ValueError\("Annual income cannot be negative."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   tax_rate = 0.0) Tj
T*
(   bracket_name = "") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if annual_income <= 250_000:) Tj
T*
(   bracket_name = "Nil Exempt") Tj
T*
(   tax_rate = 0.0) Tj
T*
(   elif annual_income <= 500_000:) Tj
T*
(   bracket_name = "Lower Middle") Tj
T*
(   tax_rate = 0.05) Tj
T*
(   elif annual_income <= 1_000_000:) Tj
T*
(   bracket_name = "Upper Middle") Tj
T*
(   tax_rate = 0.20) Tj
T*
(   else:) Tj
T*
(   bracket_name = "High Net Worth") Tj
T*
(   tax_rate = 0.30) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   calculated_tax = annual_income * tax_rate) Tj
T*
(   return {) Tj
T*
(   "Income": annual_income,) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
