BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the For Loop in Python and the Sequence Iteration Mechanism. Compare Python's for loop with traditional index-based for loops in C/Java.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Paradigm Shift: For Loop as an Iterator Consumer:) Tj
T*
(   In traditional languages like C, C++, and Java, for loops are fundamentally counter-based:) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < N; i++\) { ... }) Tj
T*
(   The programmer explicitly initializes an index, defines a loop continuation predicate, and) Tj
T*
(   increments the counter on every step.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   In Python, the for loop is fundamentally a Collection Iterator \(or foreach loop\):) Tj
T*
(   for item in iterable: ...) Tj
T*
(   Python does NOT increment a numeric index under the hood. Instead, it leverages Python's) Tj
T*
(   Iterator Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   1. Invokes iter\(iterable\) to obtain an iterator object implementing __next__\(\).) Tj
T*
(   2. On every loop iteration, calls next\(iterator\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Binds the returned value to the target loop variable.) Tj
T*
(   4. Catches the StopIteration exception automatically to terminate the loop cleanly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Advantages of Python's Sequence Iteration:) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates off-by-one boundary errors \(e.g., i <= N vs i < N\).) Tj
T*
(   - Traverses non-indexable collections seamlessly \(sets, generator streams, file handles,) Tj
T*
(   dictionary keys\).) Tj
T*
(   - Encapsulates clean, highly expressive syntax.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   # Traversing different iterable types seamlessly) Tj
T*
(   sample_list = ["Kernel", "Driver", "Filesystem"]) Tj
T*
(   sample_dict = {"PID": 1024, "State": "Running", "Priority": 1}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("Iterating over List elements:"\)) Tj
T*
(   for component in sample_list:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" Component: {component}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("Iterating over Dictionary key-value pairs:"\)) Tj
T*
(   for key, value in sample_dict.items\(\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" {key} -> {value}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Under the hood manual replication of for loop) Tj
T*
(   iterator = iter\(sample_list\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("Under-the-hood manual iterator consumption:"\)) Tj
T*
(   while True:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
