BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Nested Loops and Algorithmic Complexity. Explain how nested iteration impacts time complexity \(O\(N^2\), O\(N^3\)\) and strategies to optimize nested loops.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mechanics of Nested Loops:) Tj
T*
(   A nested loop is a loop construct placed inside the body of another loop.) Tj
T*
(   For every single iteration of the Outer Loop, the Inner Loop executes through its entire) Tj
T*
(   lifecycle from beginning to end.) Tj
T*
(   Total Iterations = \(Outer Loop Count\) * \(Inner Loop Count\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Algorithmic Complexity Implications:) Tj
T*
(   - Single Loop: O\(N\) linear time.) Tj
T*
(   - Two Nested Loops \(both of size N\): N * N = O\(N^2\) quadratic time.) Tj
T*
(   - Three Nested Loops: N * N * N = O\(N^3\) cubic time.) Tj
T*
(   As N grows \(e.g., N = 100,000 in big data or image processing\), an O\(N^2\) algorithm requires 10) Tj
T*
(   billion operations, causing severe performance degradation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Strategies for Nested Loop Optimization:) Tj
T*
(   1. Invariant Hoisting: Move calculations that do not depend on the inner loop variable out of) Tj
T*
(   the inner loop into the outer loop.) Tj
T*
(   2. Vectorization: Replace manual nested Python loops with optimized C/SIMD libraries like) Tj
T*
(   NumPy.) Tj
T*
(   3. Lookup Tables / Hash Maps: Replace inner search loops of O\(N\) with O\(1\) dictionary lookups) Tj
T*
(   to reduce total complexity from O\(N^2\) to O\(N\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration \(Matrix Multiplication\):) Tj
T*
(   def multiply_matrices\(mat_a, mat_b\):) Tj
T*
(   """Multiply two 2D matrices using 3 nested loops: O\(N^3\).""") Tj
T*
(   rows_a = len\(mat_a\)) Tj
T*
(   cols_a = len\(mat_a[0]\)) Tj
T*
(   cols_b = len\(mat_b[0]\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Initialize result matrix with zeros) Tj
T*
(   result = [[0 for _ in range\(cols_b\)] for _ in range\(rows_a\)]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Triple nested loop: O\(rows_a * cols_b * cols_a\)) Tj
T*
(   for i in range\(rows_a\):) Tj
T*
(   for j in range\(cols_b\):) Tj
T*
(   # Inner dot product accumulation) Tj
T*
(   dot_sum = 0) Tj
T*
(   for k in range\(cols_a\):) Tj
T*
(   dot_sum += mat_a[i][k] * mat_b[k][j]) Tj
T*
(   result[i][j] = dot_sum) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return result) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   A = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]) Tj
T*
(   B = [[5, 6], [7, 8]]) Tj
T*
ET

