12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Design an interactive Python program to simulate the Euclidean Algorithm for finding the Greatest Common Divisor \(GCD\) using while loops with execution trace.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis of the Euclidean Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   The Euclidean Algorithm is an ancient and remarkably efficient method for computing the) Tj
T*
(   Greatest Common Divisor \(GCD\) of two non-negative integers a and b.) Tj
T*
(   Fundamental Lemma:) Tj
T*
(   GCD\(a, b\) = GCD\(b, a % b\)) Tj
T*
(   When the remainder becomes 0, the current divisor is the exact GCD of the original two numbers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step State Transition:) Tj
T*
(   Let a = 252, b = 105:) Tj
T*
(   Iteration 1: 252 % 105 = 42 -> a becomes 105, b becomes 42.) Tj
T*
(   Iteration 2: 105 % 42 = 21 -> a becomes 42, b becomes 21.) Tj
T*
(   Iteration 3: 42 % 21 = 0 -> a becomes 21, b becomes 0.) Tj
T*
(   Termination: b == 0, therefore GCD = a = 21.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation with Detailed Trace:) Tj
T*
(   def compute_gcd_euclidean\(a: int, b: int\) -> int:) Tj
T*
(   """Compute GCD with full step-by-step state trace.""") Tj
T*
(   orig_a, orig_b = a, b) Tj
T*
(   print\("=" * 55\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Computing GCD\({a}, {b}\) via Euclidean Algorithm"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("=" * 55\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"{'Step':<8}{'Dividend \(a\)':<16}{'Divisor \(b\)':<16}{'Remainder \(a%b\)':<15}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("-" * 55\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   step = 1) Tj
T*
(   while b != 0:) Tj
T*
(   rem = a % b) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"{step:<8}{a:<16}{b:<16}{rem:<15}"\)) Tj
T*
(   a, b = b, rem # Simultaneous tuple unpacking assignment) Tj
T*
(   step += 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("-" * 55\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"GCD\({orig_a}, {orig_b}\) = {a}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("=" * 55\)) Tj
T*
(   return a) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   compute_gcd_euclidean\(252, 105\)) Tj
T*
(   compute_gcd_euclidean\(48, 18\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
