/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Design a Python program to generate Pascal's Triangle up to N rows using nested loops and combinatorial binomial coefficients.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Formulation of Pascal's Triangle:) Tj
T*
(   Pascal's Triangle is a triangular array of binomial coefficients:) Tj
T*
(   Row n, Entry k \(0 <= k <= n\) is given by:) Tj
T*
(   C\(n, k\) = n! / \(k! * \(n - k\)!\)) Tj
T*
(   Alternatively, every entry inside the triangle equals the sum of the two numbers directly above) Tj
T*
(   it:) Tj
T*
(   C\(n, k\) = C\(n - 1, k - 1\) + C\(n - 1, k\)) Tj
T*
(   with boundary conditions C\(n, 0\) = C\(n, n\) = 1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def generate_pascals_triangle\(num_rows: int\):) Tj
T*
(   """Generate Pascal's Triangle using iterative dynamic programming.""") Tj
T*
(   if num_rows <= 0:) Tj
T*
(   return []) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   triangle = []) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for r in range\(num_rows\):) Tj
T*
(   # Initialize row with 1s) Tj
T*
(   current_row = [1] * \(r + 1\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Internal entries calculated from previous row) Tj
T*
(   for c in range\(1, r\):) Tj
T*
(   current_row[c] = triangle[r - 1][c - 1] + triangle[r - 1][c]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   triangle.append\(current_row\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Format and display centered triangle) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Pascal's Triangle \({num_rows} Rows\):"\)) Tj
T*
(   max_width = len\(" ".join\(map\(str, triangle[-1]\)\)\)) Tj
T*
(   for row in triangle:) Tj
T*
(   row_str = " ".join\(f"{val:2}" for val in row\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"{row_str:^{max_width}}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
