BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a comprehensive Primality Testing program utilizing Trial Division up to sqrt\(N\) and the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Algorithms for Primality Testing:) Tj
T*
(   1. Trial Division: To determine if a single integer N is prime, test divisibility by integers) Tj
T*
(   up to floor\(sqrt\(N\)\). If no factor <= sqrt\(N\) exists, N must be prime.) Tj
T*
(   2. Sieve of Eratosthenes: To find all primes up to a large bound M, maintain a boolean array of) Tj
T*
(   size M + 1 initialized to True. Iteratively mark off multiples of each prime starting from p^2) Tj
T*
(   up to M.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def is_prime_trial\(n: int\) -> bool:) Tj
T*
(   """Test individual primality in O\(sqrt\(N\)\) time.""") Tj
T*
(   if n <= 1:) Tj
T*
(   return False) Tj
T*
(   if n <= 3:) Tj
T*
(   return True) Tj
T*
(   if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:) Tj
T*
(   return False) Tj
T*
(   # Check 6k +/- 1 optimization) Tj
T*
(   i = 5) Tj
T*
(   while i * i <= n:) Tj
T*
(   if n % i == 0 or n % \(i + 2\) == 0:) Tj
T*
(   return False) Tj
T*
(   i += 6) Tj
T*
(   return True) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def sieve_of_eratosthenes\(limit: int\) -> list:) Tj
T*
(   """Find all primes up to limit in O\(N log log N\) time.""") Tj
T*
(   is_prime = [True] * \(limit + 1\)) Tj
T*
(   is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   p = 2) Tj
T*
(   while p * p <= limit:) Tj
T*
(   if is_prime[p]:) Tj
T*
(   # Mark multiples starting from p*p) Tj
T*
(   for multiple in range\(p * p, limit + 1, p\):) Tj
T*
(   is_prime[multiple] = False) Tj
T*
(   p += 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return [num for num, prime in enumerate\(is_prime\) if prime]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
