BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the built-in enumerate\(\) and zip\(\) functions. Contrast iterating with explicit index tracking versus idiomatic parallel iteration with code.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Role of enumerate\(\) and zip\(\):) Tj
T*
(   Python philosophy \(PEP 20\) emphasizes readability and direct sequence consumption:) Tj
T*
(   - enumerate\(iterable, start=0\): Returns an iterator yielding pairs \(index, element\). Eliminates) Tj
T*
(   manual counter variables \(i = 0; i += 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - zip\(*iterables\): Aggregates elements from each of the iterables in lockstep, returning an) Tj
T*
(   iterator of tuples. Stops when the shortest input iterable is exhausted.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Antipattern vs Idiomatic Python:) Tj
T*
(   - Antipattern: for i in range\(len\(my_list\)\): process\(my_list[i]\)) Tj
T*
(   - Idiomatic: for i, item in enumerate\(my_list\): process\(i, item\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   students = ["Ananya", "Rohan", "Siddharth", "Priya"]) Tj
T*
(   scores = [92.5, 88.0, 95.0, 91.0]) Tj
T*
(   grades = ["A+", "A", "O", "A+"]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("1. Idiomatic enumerate\(\) Demonstration:"\)) Tj
T*
(   for rank, name in enumerate\(students, start=1\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" Rank #{rank}: {name}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("\\n2. Parallel Iteration with zip\(\):"\)) Tj
T*
(   for name, score, grade in zip\(students, scores, grades\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" Student: {name:<10} | Score: {score:5.1f} | Grade: {grade}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration of zip truncation behavior) Tj
T*
(   short_list = [1, 2]) Tj
T*
(   long_list = ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D']) Tj
T*
(   zipped_trunc = list\(zip\(short_list, long_list\)\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"\\n3. Zip truncation with unequal lengths: {zipped_trunc}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N\) where N is number of yielded items.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) auxiliary memory since enumerate and zip are lazy generator iterators.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
