BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the random module in depth. Detail the differences between randint, randrange, uniform, choice, choices, sample, and shuffle.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture of Python's random Module:) Tj
T*
(   The random module implements the Mersenne Twister \(MT19937\) PRNG, providing a massive period of) Tj
T*
(   2^19937 - 1 with 623-dimensional equidistribution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comprehensive Functional Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   1. random.randint\(a, b\): Returns random integer N such that a <= N <= b \(Both endpoints) Tj
T*
(   inclusive!\).) Tj
T*
(   2. random.randrange\(start, stop[, step]\): Returns random item from range\(start, stop, step\)) Tj
T*
(   \(Stop is exclusive!\).) Tj
T*
(   3. random.uniform\(a, b\): Returns continuous floating-point number N such that a <= N <= b.) Tj
T*
(   4. random.choice\(seq\): Selects a single random item from non-empty sequence seq.) Tj
T*
(   5. random.choices\(population, weights=None, k=1\): Selects k items with replacement \(items can) Tj
T*
(   repeat\). Supports weighted probabilities.) Tj
T*
(   6. random.sample\(population, k\): Selects k unique items without replacement \(items never) Tj
T*
(   repeat\). Raises ValueError if k > len\(population\).) Tj
T*
(   7. random.shuffle\(x\): Randomly permutes mutable sequence x in-place in O\(N\) time via the) Tj
T*
(   Fisher-Yates shuffle algorithm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import random) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   random.seed\(101\) # Seed for reproducible verification) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"randint\(1, 10\): {random.randint\(1, 10\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"randrange\(0, 50, 5\): {random.randrange\(0, 50, 5\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"uniform\(1.5, 9.5\): {random.uniform\(1.5, 9.5\):.3f}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   deck = ["Ace", "King", "Queen", "Jack", "Ten"]) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"choice\(deck\): {random.choice\(deck\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"choices\(k=3, repl\): {random.choices\(deck, k=3\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"sample\(k=3, norepl\): {random.sample\(deck, k=3\)}"\)) Tj
T*
ET

