BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the secrets module introduced in Python 3.6. Why is random unsuitable for security, and how does secrets generate cryptographically secure tokens?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Why the standard random module is insecure:) Tj
T*
(   The Mersenne Twister PRNG in random is designed purely for statistical simulation and gaming.) Tj
T*
(   It is completely deterministic. By observing just 624 consecutive 32-bit outputs, an attacker) Tj
T*
(   can reconstruct the internal 19,937-bit state vector and predict all future 'random' numbers) Tj
T*
(   with 100% accuracy!) Tj
T*
(   Using random for session tokens, passwords, or cryptographic keys creates critical security) Tj
T*
(   vulnerabilities \(CWE-330\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Cryptographic Randomness via secrets:) Tj
T*
(   Introduced in Python 3.6 \(PEP 506\), the secrets module accesses operating-system-level entropy) Tj
T*
(   sources \(CryptGenRandom on Windows, /dev/urandom or getrandom\(\) on Linux\):) Tj
T*
(   - secrets.choice\(seq\): Cryptographically secure random selection.) Tj
T*
(   - secrets.randbelow\(n\): Cryptographically secure integer in [0, n\).) Tj
T*
(   - secrets.token_bytes\(nbytes\): Raw cryptographically secure random bytes.) Tj
T*
(   - secrets.token_hex\(nbytes\): Hexadecimal-encoded secure token.) Tj
T*
(   - secrets.token_urlsafe\(nbytes\): Base64-URL-safe token \(ideal for password reset links\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import secrets) Tj
T*
(   import string) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def generate_secure_password\(length=16\) -> str:) Tj
T*
(   """Generate cryptographically secure high-entropy password.""") Tj
T*
(   alphabet = string.ascii_letters + string.digits + "!@#$%^&*\(\)-_=+") Tj
T*
(   # Cryptographically secure random selection) Tj
T*
(   password = "".join\(secrets.choice\(alphabet\) for _ in range\(length\)\)) Tj
T*
(   return password) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def generate_api_tokens\(\):) Tj
T*
(   """Generate secure URL tokens for authentication.""") Tj
T*
(   auth_token = secrets.token_hex\(16\) # 32 hex characters) Tj
T*
(   reset_token = secrets.token_urlsafe\(24\) # URL-safe Base64) Tj
T*
(   return auth_token, reset_token) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Secure Password: {generate_secure_password\(14\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   auth_tok, reset_tok = generate_api_tokens\(\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Hex Auth Token: {auth_tok}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"URL Reset Token: {reset_tok}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
ET

