BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Design a Python program to compute the Taylor Series expansion of sin\(x\) and cos\(x\) up to N terms using while loops and factorial accumulation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Formulation of Taylor Series:) Tj
T*
(   The Maclaurin series expansions about x = 0 \(with x in radians\) are:) Tj
T*
(   sin\(x\) = Sum_{n=0}^{inf} \(-1\)^n * \(x^\(2n + 1\)\) / \(2n + 1\)! = x - x^3/3! + x^5/5! - ...) Tj
T*
(   cos\(x\) = Sum_{n=0}^{inf} \(-1\)^n * \(x^\(2n\)\) / \(2n\)! = 1 - x^2/2! + x^4/4! - ...) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   import math) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def taylor_sin\(x_deg: float, tolerance=1e-10, max_terms=50\) -> float:) Tj
T*
(   # Convert degrees to radians) Tj
T*
(   x = math.radians\(x_deg\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   term = x # Initial term n=0: x^1 / 1!) Tj
T*
(   sin_sum = term) Tj
T*
(   n = 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   while abs\(term\) > tolerance and n < max_terms:) Tj
T*
(   # Efficient recurrence relation: term_next = -term * \(x^2\) / \(\(2n\)*\(2n+1\)\)) Tj
T*
(   term = -term * \(x ** 2\) / \(\(2 * n\) * \(2 * n + 1\)\)) Tj
T*
(   sin_sum += term) Tj
T*
(   n += 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return sin_sum, n) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification against math.sin\(\)) Tj
T*
(   angle = 30.0 # sin\(30 deg\) = 0.5000) Tj
T*
(   computed_val, num_terms = taylor_sin\(angle\)) Tj
T*
(   actual_val = math.sin\(math.radians\(angle\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Taylor Series Calculation for sin\({angle} degrees\):"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" Computed Value: {computed_val:.10f}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" math.sin Value: {actual_val:.10f}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" Terms Computed: {num_terms} | Absolute Error: {abs\(computed_val - actual_val\):.2e}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(K\) where K is number of terms needed for convergence \(typically < 15) Tj
T*
(   terms\).) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) auxiliary variables.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
