(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Structural Pattern Matching \(match-case\) introduced in Python 3.10 \(PEP 634\). Compare with C-style switch-case and traditional if-elif-else.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Paradigm Shift: PEP 634 Structural Pattern Matching:) Tj
T*
(   Introduced in Python 3.10, match-case is fundamentally more powerful than C-style switch-case) Tj
T*
(   statements:) Tj
T*
(   - C switch: Only compares a primitive integer/char against static compile-time constants.) Tj
T*
(   Requires explicit break statements to avoid fall-through.) Tj
T*
(   - Python match-case: Inspects both value and structure \(shapes of sequences, objects,) Tj
T*
(   dictionaries\), extracts variables, and matches against patterns with optional guard clauses) Tj
T*
(   \(if\). No break is required; execution never falls through.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Pattern Types Supported:) Tj
T*
(   - Literal patterns: case 404:) Tj
T*
(   - Capture patterns: case \(x, y\):) Tj
T*
(   - Wildcard pattern: case _: \(Matches anything; default branch\)) Tj
T*
(   - OR patterns: case 401 | 403:) Tj
T*
(   - Guard clauses: case x if x > 0:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   def handle_rest_api_event\(event: dict\) -> str:) Tj
T*
(   """Process API requests using structural pattern matching.""") Tj
T*
(   match event:) Tj
T*
(   case {"action": "login", "user": username, "status": "success"}:) Tj
T*
(   return f"User '{username}' logged in successfully.") Tj
T*
(   case {"action": "login", "user": username, "status": "failed", "attempts": n} if n >= 3:) Tj
T*
(   return f"ALERT: Account '{username}' locked due to {n} failed attempts!") Tj
T*
(   case {"action": "fetch", "resource_id": int\(rid\)}:) Tj
T*
(   return f"Fetching resource record #{rid}.") Tj
T*
(   case {"action": "logout"}:) Tj
T*
(   return "User logged out.") Tj
T*
(   case _:) Tj
T*
(   return "Unknown event payload received.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration) Tj
T*
(   print\(handle_rest_api_event\({"action": "login", "user": "Hariom", "status": "success"}\)\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(handle_rest_api_event\({"action": "login", "user": "Admin", "status": "failed",) Tj
T*
(   "attempts": 4}\)\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(handle_rest_api_event\({"action": "fetch", "resource_id": 1042}\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
