(   Ratio of Circle Area to Square Area:) Tj
T*
(   Area_Circle / Area_Square = \(pi * R^2\) / \(4 * R^2\) = pi / 4.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   pi = 4 * \(Points_Inside_Circle / Total_Points\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Simulation Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   1. Generate N uniform random points \(x, y\) in the range [-1.0, 1.0].) Tj
T*
(   2. For each point, evaluate Euclidean distance from origin: dist_sq = x^2 + y^2.) Tj
T*
(   3. If dist_sq <= 1.0, the point falls inside the inscribed circle.) Tj
T*
(   4. Estimate pi = 4.0 * inside_count / N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   import random) Tj
T*
(   import math) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def monte_carlo_pi_estimator\(num_samples=500_000, seed=42\):) Tj
T*
(   random.seed\(seed\)) Tj
T*
(   inside_circle = 0) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for _ in range\(num_samples\):) Tj
T*
(   x = random.uniform\(-1.0, 1.0\)) Tj
T*
(   y = random.uniform\(-1.0, 1.0\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if \(x * x\) + \(y * y\) <= 1.0:) Tj
T*
(   inside_circle += 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   estimated_pi = 4.0 * inside_circle / num_samples) Tj
T*
(   error = abs\(estimated_pi - math.pi\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("=" * 55\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(" MONTE CARLO PI SIMULATION EXPERIMENT "\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("=" * 55\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Total Random Samples \(N\): {num_samples:,}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Points Inside Circle \(M\): {inside_circle:,}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Estimated Pi Value: {estimated_pi:.6f}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Actual math.pi Reference: {math.pi:.6f}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Absolute Estimation Error: {error:.6f} \({error / math.pi * 100:.4f}%\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("=" * 55\)) Tj
T*
(   return estimated_pi) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Run verification) Tj
T*
(   monte_carlo_pi_estimator\(num_samples=250_000\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N\) linear time proportional to sample count.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) auxiliary memory registers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
